    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0762" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/172</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-28">October 28, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1723</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">L. N. No. 1843</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    communication addressed to you from the Secretary General of the League of
                    Nations dated October 27, 1930 (C.L.292(b)1930.XI)<anchor n="75"
                        xml:id="d511-f1"/> in which he informs you of the decision of the Council of
                    the League of Nations to convert the Conference on the Limitation of the
                    Manufacture of Narcotic Drugs which was originally confined to a certain number
                    of States into a General Conference for all States, the date of this Conference
                    having been fixed as May 27, 1931.</p>
                <p>The communication further informs you of the list of countries invited to the
                    Conference of Manufacturing States to be held in Great Britain beginning October
                    27, 1931 [<hi rendition="#italic">1930</hi>] These countries are: France,
                    Germany, Great Britain, India, Italy, Japan, Netherlands, Switzerland, Turkey,
                    United States of America, the Union of Socialist Soviet Republics.</p>
                <p>There are enclosed with the communication copy of the Minutes of the Sixtieth
                    Session and Sixty-first Session of the Council, the Report submitted to the
                    Fifth Committee of the Eleventh Assembly on the traffic in opium and other
                    dangerous drugs, together with a copy of the report of the Fifth Committee to
                    the Assembly on the same question.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont Moffat</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
